          {
            "x": 2.178649237472767,
            "y": 12.910611231371064,
            "width": 92.73743016759778,
            "height": 86.09271523178808,
            "action": {
              "library": "H5P.AdvancedText 1.1",
              "params": {
                "text": "<p><strong>Political Ideology and Achievements</strong><br>\nBenazir Bhutto advocated for democracy and women's rights in a largely conservative society. She was recognized for her charismatic leadership and efforts to modernize Pakistan. Her achievements include expanding health care and education and advocating for women in politics, despite resistance from conservative factions within Pakistan.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Assassination and Legacy</strong><br>\nOn December 27, 2007, Benazir Bhutto was assassinated in a terrorist attack after a political rally in Rawalpindi, Pakistan. Her death led to widespread national mourning and international condemnation. The loss of Benazir Bhutto was felt not just in Pakistan but worldwide, as she had become a symbol of the struggle for democracy and women's empowerment.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Impact on Pakistan and the World</strong><br>\nBenazir Bhutto's life and career had a profound impact on Pakistan's political landscape. She is remembered for her attempts to democratize Pakistan and her role as a pioneer for women in Muslim-majority countries. Her tragic death has been a constant reminder of the volatile nature of Pakistani politics and the challenges faced by those who seek to change it.</p>\n"
              },
